    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **James Wood**, whose 78.42 score makes him the undisputed engine of the offense. Facing Giolito (5.37 xERA), **James Wood** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill advantage and a premium spot in the order, positioning him to capitalize on his elite .384 xwOBA. We are also leaning heavily on **Austin Riley** (65.80) and **Josh Naylor** (65.73), both of whom provide high-floor production despite moderate pitcher matchups. While **Corbin Carroll** (63.34) faces a tough assignment in Kirby (3.46 xERA), his stolen base upside remains critical; his 87% steal-probability against the Kirby/catcher battery keeps his score elevated despite the clear strikeout risk.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (45.93), who barely missed the cut. While he possesses the talent to start, his 15% platoon disadvantage against the lefty Gore proved too steep a hurdle compared to the efficiency profiles of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte**. Both **Tyler Soderstrom** (61.50) and **Henry Bolte** (58.91) are boosted by favorable park conditions and advantageous platoon splits against Rod\u00f3n, squeezing **Vinnie Pasquantino** out of the UTIL spot. We are monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero** (54.02) closely; while his park-adjusted metrics remain viable, his bottom-of-the-order assignment and the challenge of navigating an elite catcher arm like Severino's make him our most volatile start.\n\nThe primary risk today involves the top of our pitching matchups. Both **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** are forced to contend with Kirby\u2019s 3.46 xERA, which suppresses their respective scores significantly. Furthermore, we are watching the efficiency of **Zach McKinstry** (46.54) and **Cole Young** (46.04), both of whom are currently trending toward the lower end of our starting threshold. Should weather or late lineup shifts negatively impact these secondary bats, we are prepared to pivot to more favorable platoons, though for now, the data suggests maximizing volume across the board to chase those high-value steals.",
